WEBVTT

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.280
In the midst of your sadness...

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.190
You made Mama die.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:16.910
What does that mean?

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.480
Dammit!

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.890
Kaito...

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.970
Are you okay, Kaito?

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.100
First Cubik, now Kaito.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.470
Two losses in a row.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.970
We're up against the wall.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.090
N..Now's not the time to talk like that!

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.690
We can't lose any of the next three games.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.060
Even if I don't lose,

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.100
I'm worried about...

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.390
The next game with Ana,

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.860
and the guy who fights again in the last battle:

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:53.990
Kaito.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.960
The way he is now, Kaito ain't much use.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:01.930
What'd you say?!

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:02.750
Kaito!

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.720
Normally, there's no way you'd lose to a punk like that.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.280
Am I wrong?

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.490
Kaito!

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.440
Wait, Kaito!

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.440
Here's a charm for you, Kaito:

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.400
Happy-smiley.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.930
Lost

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.050
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.970
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.850
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:02.230
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.940
Found

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:08.150
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:12.660
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.450
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.580
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:21.920
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.790
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.500
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.880
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.090
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.470
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:35.930
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.640
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.470
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:42.310
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.480
It's now or never

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.560
That is what they say

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.650
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:51.320
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.490
That is what they say

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.660
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.160
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.370
That is what they say

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.790
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:07.990
I Want to Give You Happy-Smiley

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.180
Hey!

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.430
Wait, Kaito!

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.520
Kaito, come on!

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.520
Kaito...

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:32.380
Why were you so cruel to Kaito?

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:35.890
You think he would have lost if he'd shown

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.050
the same strength as always?

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.530
Well...

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:44.940
Still, for him to get so flustered...

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:49.500
The wounds in Kaito's heart 'cuz of his parents

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.750
ain't healed yet, is that it?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.010
Damn, these Orpheus Order guys
use some dirty tricks.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.390
This food they've prepared for us is awesome though.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.350
And? Where's Kaito?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.020
He hasn't come back yet.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.190
Nonoha either.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.330
I see.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.510
Dude, you can eat, huh?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.720
I can't provide good support on an empty stomach.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.270
Yoshio, you should charge your

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.880
batteries while you can too.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:41.450
In any case, where did Ana run off to?

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:45.130
Kaito and Nonoha ain't back yet either.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.060
To think that Kaito still has suffering
I didn't know about...

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.990
And his face shows that suffering.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.700
But there's nothing I can do for him.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.730
That's just so sad...

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.910
I, Ana, think you get a charm too.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.790
Fluffy-smiley!

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:21.460
Ana...

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:28.080
Still, other people's intentions put
their eyes firmly on Kaito.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.640
But their gazes aren't just round,

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.070
or gentle.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:42.230
They're grating, thorny, sometimes piercing.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.450
Yet, Kaito doesn't avoid their eyes.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:53.660
So, I want Kaito to have some soft and fluffy too.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:59.030
The soft and fluffy that I, Ana, got from that person.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.040
"That person"?

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:04.510
The person who got rid of
the spell that was cast on me.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.610
The person who freed me, Ana,

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.800
from inside that heavy shell.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.850
My precious Eve.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.220
Eve?

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.830
Eve is my older sister.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:21.440
I, Ana, had long forgotten how to smile,

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.940
but she gave me a fluffy painting as a present.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:37.650
When I, Ana, got that fluffy painting from Eve,

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:40.000
it made my heart soft.

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:45.380
And thanks to that softness, I found happy-smiley.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:46.850
That's why...

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:48.610
So this is where you've been.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.440
It's almost time for the next game to start, yes?

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:18.010
Come on, let's go to the rink, Pinochle.

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:20.370
Uh, yeah.

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:27.920
Where's Mizerka?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.270
Big Sis went to go see her opponent.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:33.420
What for?

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.760
She said she had something to confirm.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.100
Something to confirm?

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:43.610
Just what do you want to confirm?

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:47.320
Have you been well, Miss Stuffed Animal?

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.250
Where do you get off?!

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.950
Sorry, I don't have time for you right now.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.490
H..Hey!

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.420
What do you want to confirm?

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.200
Hey, are you listening?

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:02.030
I thought it might be, but...

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.890
Yes, sure enough, it's you.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:06.230
Finished!

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:07.920
What? What is it?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.680
You seem rather confident to be drawing pictures.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.630
You've completely forgotten that you lost to me

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:17.560
in the last game, have you?

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.180
Huh?

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:25.230
The third game shall now begin.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:30.230
The opponents are Mr. Ana Gram and Miss Mizerka.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:32.740
We're countin' on ya, Ana!

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.270
Leave it to me!

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.660
I, Ana, will do my best!

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:41.390
I, Ana, will try my utmost!

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.290
I said we're up against the wall.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.450
Is that guy gonna be okay?

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:43.680
If it were my turn...

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:49.040
Even if you won, Ana's turn would still come around.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.420
Sooner if not later.

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:52.760
Anyway, where's Kaito?

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.080
It's not like if he were here,

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.000
he could give Ana help from the bench.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.550
It's against the rules.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.090
More to the point,

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:05.270
I don't think he's capable of that right now.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:14.330
Huh? He's not here?

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:19.670
I guess he's no big deal after all, Kaito Daimon.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:26.680
It's starting.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:32.020
The first move goes to Mr. Ana Gram, player from

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:33.840
the team with fewer victories.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.200
Now then, third game...

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:36.840
Play.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:46.560
Well, I'm very sorry for keeping you so late,

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:51.820
but please continue analyzing the data, Maze.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.940
Still, in our

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:59.720
2,000-year history, the POG hasn't been able to collect

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:03.140
many Armlets of Orpheus.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.540
How did they acquire all theirs?

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:08.950
Maybe there are many

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:14.210
Armlets out there that still haven't been discovered.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:15.970
Or...

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.640
It couldn't be, right?

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.660
All right, make your next move.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:44.560
This time, I'll probably...

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:45.650
go here!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.580
This is a good move!

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:49.360
Why?

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:52.380
It doesn't seem a particularly
effective move to my eyes.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:57.300
Well, I feel like a little bird is calling me.

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:00.950
Look, we're up against the wall!

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:02.850
Make it happen, Ana!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.310
Then, I...

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:13.860
Oh, my, a delicious scent is coming from over there.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:19.280
I shall strike right back.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.070
A nice wind is blowing from over here.

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.700
Is that person for real?

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.330
He's just going around the rink's circumference.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.290
It can't be.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.880
Going 'round in circles is fun!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.170
Indeed.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.210
As I'd heard, you're quite interesting.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.530
Free-spirited people like you...

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:51.020
I can't stand.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:18.510
In the midst of your sadness...

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:21.090
You made Mama die.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.540
That's right, it was a rainy day.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:39.410
I saw him...

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:41.530
them!

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:14.680
I never dreamed that was Freecell's mother.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:18.500
His mom really died?

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.950
I finally found you.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:30.290
I'm still gonna go 'round and round!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.910
Do what you want.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.030
So, even though the game has begun,

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:41.490
Kaito Daimon fails to appear?

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:45.410
Whether he's here or not doesn't matter, does it?

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:49.420
It's still an interesting game.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:50.520
True enough.

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:56.350
Mizerka, who fights the most orthodox of us all,

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.210
versus her polar opposite, Ana Gram.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:01.420
How will things turn out?

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.810
Thrilling, isn't it?

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.950
Y..Yes, that's right.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.990
Why not keep screwing around like that?

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:13.620
I'm going to get ready to finish this.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.980
This is fun too!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:24.030
Say, don't you think Mizerka is "off" somehow?

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:28.990
People like you...

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:33.440
People who live their lives however they want...

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.200
I really hate them!

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.390
Instinctively...

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:39.190
From the bottom of my heart, I can't accept you!

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.780
I, Ana, will get one too!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.280
You're selfish, self-centered, conceited...

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:48.440
You care nothing for the trouble you cause!

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:53.660
Sometimes, being right in the middle feels good, huh?

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.830
You've confused freedom with selfishness.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:59.460
Your life is frivolous, nothing more!

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:04.100
As proof of that, even now,
you're defending Kaito Daimon.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:07.990
This is bad!

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.010
At this rate, Ana will...

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:13.500
Victory will be celebrated in three moves,

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.200
but...

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:18.760
Big Sis is always so collected.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:20.600
Why is she...

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:25.480
I can't understand it at all.

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:28.660
He drove Freecell's mother to the grave,

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:30.520
yet he paid it no mind,

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:33.470
went on living his own life as if nothing had happened.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:37.200
You're allies with the lowest form of scum!

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.660
She called Kaito "scum"?!

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:45.540
Probably, those words just now...

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.550
That person... Mizerka's turn...

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.600
He stopped it!

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.440
Those words just now...

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:04.550
I, Ana, won't allow them.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.900
Hey, where are we going?

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.580
Just come on!

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.970
Won't allow them?

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.820
That's my line.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.410
Or do you have some explanation
that can sway my mind?

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:24.130
Why do you cover for that scum?

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:28.020
The way Kaito is now, it's just like...

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:37.510
I'm gonna teach you a great charm, Ana.

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:41.030
No matter how cold your heart may get,

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:43.430
it will make it nice and warm.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.560
It's that kind of charm.

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:50.730
Happy-smiley, fluffy-smiley.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:04.290
And now, it's my turn.

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:10.580
Look, what the hell?!

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:11.950
Come on!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.640
Look!

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:03.490
You're not alone, Kaito.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:08.230
Ana... The others... Me...
We're all with you.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.690
No matter what happens, we're together.

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:13.730
So...

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:27.500
I, Ana, want to cherish the happy-smiley Eve gave me.

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:32.630
Acting incomprehensibly again...

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:36.040
So, Da Vinci is back to normal?

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:37.380
Big Sis...

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:39.890
Yes...

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.890
You keep mocking people relentlessly, don't you?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.750
No, Ana, that's just the same as before!

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.360
Gammon?

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:57.120
I want to cherish that happy-smiley.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:01.160
Then, you should all softly, gently...

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:03.410
commit suicide together!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.820
This is the end.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:08.530
It really is.

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:12.420
You made a good run of it, but...

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.380
Too bad, Mizerka.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:20.360
I, Ana, think...

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.560
You were close, but the answer is...

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.730
Happy-smiley, fluffy-smiley.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:34.230
Two turns left, and Ana wins!

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:35.480
No way!

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:36.730
It can't be!

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.490
He read her moves?

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:50.330
It's settled.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.850
Third game, winner:

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.090
Mr. Ana!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.590
Yoohoo!

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:01.560
That was great, Ana!

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:04.630
By bein' persistent and circling the outside

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:06.840
of the lanes, your totally distracted her.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:08.560
Great job!

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.480
Oh, so it was a strategy.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:12.980
Huh?

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.440
How unsightly.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.650
Not like you, is it?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:21.200
To get that worked up?

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:25.160
Big Sister, your punishment will follow.

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:28.030
We've only suffered one loss.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:49.010
Souji Jikukawa's guess may have been accurate.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:56.080
The Orpheus Order is attempting to
enter forbidden territory,

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:58.980
places even we POG feared to tread.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:19.240
Thank you, Ana.

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:22.670
I get happy just looking at it.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.120
But I...

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:28.850
Kaito, make it warm.

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:37.940
That young man's smile is frozen.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.570
So, Kaito, warm it up.

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:47.910
I'm sure you're the one who can

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:50.530
give him happy-smiley.

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:05.440
That's why...

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:07.970
I want to know the truth.

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:14.310
He really is just as Eve said.

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:20.230
Him, and his friends...

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:22.460
I hate them all!

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:04.010
It's been so boring, huh?

00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:05.710
What suddenly happened to you, Airi?

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:07.880
Your friends have had lots of air time recently,

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:10.010
so I thought maybe now I'm needed.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:11.320
O..Oh, really?

00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:12.760
The foil and straight man,

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:14.390
telling punch line
after punch line, after punch line!

00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:15.760
I'm needed!

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:19.100
Hey there! We're Nonoha and Airi!

00:24:19.100 --> 00:24:21.600
Next time, "The Truth Behind the Smile"

00:24:20.080 --> 00:24:26.540
The Truth Behind the Smile

00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:24.090
You're not appearing next week, are you?

00:24:24.090 --> 00:24:25.760
But, why not?!
